%% Figure 2: Global UML Use Case Diagram (Global Use Case Diagram)
%% JC2001 Group 5 / Smart Study Assistant
%% Notes:
%%   1. <<include>> / <<extend>> stereotypes are rendered with ASCII angle brackets. Mermaid's HTML label
%%      sanitizer strips <...> in edge labels as unknown tags, so the source uses the monospace placeholders
%%      [[ST_INCLUDE]] / [[ST_EXTEND]], which tools/render_figures.mjs replaces with the real stereotypes at export
%%      time while correcting label widths accordingly; when previewing directly in mermaid.live, replace them manually.
%%   2. Relationship direction follows the UML 2.5 specification: include relationship (<<include>>) goes from base use case -> included use case;
%%      extend relationship (<<extend>>) goes from extending use case -> base use case.
%%   3. The dashed box marks the system boundary; status markers are listed below.
%%      [Implemented] delivered in the current PoC; [Frontend-computed] no backend endpoint; [Planned] future iteration.
flowchart LR
    Student(["University Student<br/>(Student)"])

    subgraph Core["Smart Study Assistant Core Function Domain (System Boundary)"]
        direction LR
        UC02["<b>UC-02 Targeted Self-Assessment Practice</b><br/>[Implemented]"]
